From 1ff0c2d490005470bbbfeed24da21bb603a490e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: okhsunrog <me@okhsunrog.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:07:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] efi/libstub: Preserve the initrd table across kexec

The inherited EFI table is consumed and zeroed again by a kexec kernel. EFI loader data can already contain the new initramfs at that address. Allocate the table in ACPI reclaim memory so that it remains reserved across handoff.

Adapt the allocation fix proposed by Sebastien WENSKE to the Linux 7.2.9 TPM hibernation port. Reproduced with signed kexec under integrity Lockdown on both TIS and CRB VM fixtures.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-efi/20261012133712.618913-1-sebastien@wenske.fr/
---
 drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/efi-stub-helper.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/efi-stub-helper.c b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/efi-stub-helper.c
index 996313f..1318f8c 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/efi-stub-helper.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/efi-stub-helper.c
@@ -647,8 +647,12 @@ efi_status_t efi_load_initrd(efi_loaded_image_t *image,
 				     EFISTUB_EVT_INITRD) == EFI_SUCCESS)
 		efi_info("Measured initrd data into PCR 9\n");
 
-	status = efi_bs_call(allocate_pool, EFI_LOADER_DATA, sizeof(initrd),
-			     (void **)&tbl);
+	/*
+	 * Configuration tables survive kexec. Keep this one out of loader data:
+	 * a later kernel clears it again, after loader data may be reused.
+	 */
+	status = efi_bs_call(allocate_pool, EFI_ACPI_RECLAIM_MEMORY,
+			     sizeof(initrd), (void **)&tbl);
 	if (status != EFI_SUCCESS)
 		goto free_initrd;
 
-- 
